-- Explain the shared shop controls in the existing product-visibility task.
-- Replace its troubleshooting paragraph rather than adding another section.
UPDATE public.help_articles
SET body = replace(body,
  $old$<p>Confirm the product status is <strong>Published</strong>, then clear category filters and search for the exact name or URL handle. Published status controls whether the product appears in the catalogue. A hidden category is removed from category navigation, but does not by itself hide a published product from the full catalogue. Zero tracked stock also does not hide the product; it changes whether customers can buy it and normally shows it as sold out unless backorders are allowed.</p>$old$,
  $new$<p>Confirm the product status is <strong>Published</strong>, then open the full shop and clear search text. Shop and collection pages include <strong>Filter</strong> and <strong>Sort by</strong> controls on every theme. Select Filter to choose <strong>In stock only</strong> or a minimum and maximum price, review the matching product count, then press the button showing that count to apply your choices. On a phone the same controls open in a panel at the bottom of the screen. Active filters appear as removable chips; use <strong>Clear all</strong> when multiple filters are active to remove them together. Sort by featured order, price, newest or name, and use <strong>Load more</strong> to reveal products beyond the first 24.</p><p>Published status controls whether a product appears in the catalogue. A hidden category is removed from category navigation, but does not by itself hide a published product from the full shop. Zero tracked stock normally shows the product as sold out unless backorders are allowed; <strong>In stock only</strong> excludes products that cannot be bought. Clear that filter and any price limits when checking whether a published product is missing.</p>$new$),
  updated_at = now()
WHERE slug = 'publish-feature-and-improve-a-product-for-search'
  AND status = 'published';
